; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Emergency Room
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     priority queue, sorted insert, lists, simulation
; SUMMARY:  A priority queue keeps patients sorted by how urgent they are, so the doctor always sees the most urgent one next.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   In an ordinary queue, whoever comes first is served first. In an
;   emergency room, a broken leg goes before a sore thumb even if it
;   arrived later. Each patient is a pair [urgency name], and the
;   waiting list is always kept sorted with the highest urgency at
;   the front. The turtle draws the waiting room after every event.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. The events list at the bottom says who arrives and
;   when the doctor is free. Edit it to tell a different story.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a priority queue built from a sorted list
;   * a recursive insert that finds the right spot
;   * patients with equal urgency still keep arrival order
;   * running a list of events with FOREACH and CASE
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add a second doctor who serves the same queue.
;   * Raise every waiting patient's urgency by one each turn, so
;     nobody waits forever. This is called aging.
; ============================================================

make "waiting []

; Put a patient in place. We walk past everyone whose urgency is
; greater OR EQUAL, so a newcomer goes behind others of the same level.
to pqinsert :p :list
  if emptyp :list [output (list :p)]
  if (first :p) > (first first :list) [output fput :p :list]
  output fput first :list pqinsert :p butfirst :list
end

to arrive :urgency :name
  make "waiting pqinsert (list :urgency :name) :waiting
  print (sentence :name [arrives with urgency] :urgency)
end

to treat
  if emptyp :waiting [print [The doctor has a cup of tea.] stop]
  localmake "p first :waiting
  make "waiting butfirst :waiting
  print (sentence [The doctor sees] last :p)
end

; Urgency 5 is red and 1 is green, so the room reads at a glance.
to urgencycolor :u
  output item :u [[90 190 90] [170 210 60] [240 200 40] [240 130 40] [220 50 50]]
end

to drawroom
  clean
  penup setxy -360 250 setpencolor "black
  label [Waiting room, next patient on the left]
  localmake "x -360
  foreach :waiting [
    penup setxy :x 200 setheading 90
    filled urgencycolor first ? [repeat 2 [fd 100 rt 90 fd 60 rt 90]]
    setpencolor "black setxy :x + 10 170 label last ?
    setxy :x + 10 150 label sentence "level first ?
    make "x :x + 110
  ]
end

to run.events :events
  foreach :events [
    case first ? [
      [[arrive] arrive item 2 ? item 3 ?]
      [[treat] treat]
    ]
    drawroom
    wait 40
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
run.events [
  [arrive 2 Ola] [arrive 1 Pip] [arrive 4 Quin] [treat]
  [arrive 5 Rosa] [arrive 2 Sid] [arrive 3 Tam] [treat]
  [arrive 4 Uma] [treat] [treat] [treat] [treat] [treat] [treat]
]
